Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The failed strategy opened constrained mode almost immediately and then relied
// on constrained token generation to synthesize arithmetic expressions from
// scratch. In practice, that caused the model to enter `<<` before producing any
// natural-language reasoning and then get stuck in low-quality constrained text,
// often never reaching a complete prefix that could be closed. The evaluation
// explicitly shows both failure modes: opening too early and leaving spans
// unterminated.
//
// This revision adopts a much more conservative policy tailored to the task:
//
// 1. Outside constrained mode, default to ordinary unconstrained generation and
//    strongly penalize delimiter tokens so accidental raw `<<` / `>>` almost
//    never appear.
// 2. We only deliberately open a constrained span when the immediately previous
//    generated token is one of a small set of arithmetic cue tokens such as "=",
//    "+", "-", "*", "/", or "^". This delays `<<` until the surrounding prose
//    has likely introduced a computation.
// 3. Once inside constrained mode, we generate at most one arithmetic token and
//    then, as soon as the parser reports completeness, we close immediately on
//    the next iteration. This keeps spans short and greatly reduces the chance
//    of getting stuck.
// 4. We never open unless at least two steps remain (one to open, one to make
//    progress inside), and while inside we reserve budget so we do not extend a
//    span when there would be no room left to close it.
// 5. If already inside on entry, we prioritize either closing a complete span or
//    taking a single constrained step toward completion; otherwise we stop rather
//    than risk an unterminated segment.
//
// Compared with the previous attempt, the key change is that constrained spans
// are no longer the default generation mode. They are rare, cue-triggered, and
// aggressively closed, which directly addresses both observed evaluation
// failures while still ensuring the output can contain `<< >>` arithmetic
// computations when the model naturally reaches a calculation site.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In unconstrained branches we stay outside constrained mode,
//   so the implication is vacuous. The open branch uses OpenConstrainedSpan,
//   which sets the constrained content to [] and therefore valid. The
//   constrained-append branch obtains a parser-valid token from ConstrainedStep
//   and then uses AppendConstrainedToken to extend the tracked constrained
//   prefix, preserving validity. The close branch exits constrained mode, so the
